1
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:13,212
… and some people think that only older people – like me – can be inventors.

2
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,960
But they’re wrong, you know?

3
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:32,300
Here’s one example – a young man in South Africa, only 17 years old, saw a problem with water quality and he invented a gel that people can use to wash, to have a bath, even if there is no water.

4
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,460
He was only 17!

5
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:38,340
So, you guys out there, you shouldn’t wait.

6
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:41,400
Just go ahead and do it, OK?

7
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:46,160
So now, we don’t have much time, any questions?

8
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,360
Did the boy in South Africa get rich?

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,140
I really don’t know.

10
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:52,440
I hope so!

11
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:54,280
But that’s not the point.

12
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:58,640
He invented something that made other people’s lives better.

13
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,700
He didn’t think: how can I get rich?

14
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,100
He thought: how can I help people?

15
00:01:05,829 --> 00:01:08,260
And that’s the place you should start.

16
00:01:08,801 --> 00:01:12,609
You should start with an idea to help other people.

17
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:16,980
To make lives easier and, hopefully, better.

18
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,860
I’ve got lots of ideas for inventions.

19
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,880
Oh? Like what?

20
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:26,020
Well, I don’t want to say.

21
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,440
Good for you!

22
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,220
Be very careful.

23
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:33,180
You should only talk to people that you trust, OK?

24
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:38,820
But another thing: you say you’ve got lots of ideas, and that’s great.

25
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:43,200
But don’t try to work on all of them at the same time.

26
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:48,205
You should say to yourself: which idea is the best one?

27
00:01:48,205 --> 00:01:52,460
And then you should try to work more on that idea.

28
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:54,860
And should I forget the other ones?

29
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:55,780
No, no, no!

30
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:57,120
Absolutely not.

31
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:00,480
I mean, I’m sure you won’t forget them anyway.

32
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:03,380
Yes, another question?

33
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,852
Is being an inventor a job?

34
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,780
I mean, should I leave school and just start inventing things?

35
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:13,660
Hahaha, it sounds like a good idea, right?

36
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:20,720
But to start, when you leave school, I think you should get a job and invent things as a hobby.

37
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:21,520
Why?

38
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:24,800
Well, you have to live, don’t you?

39
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:31,580
And maybe your first invention isn’t successful, so where is the money for you to live?

40
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:38,140
No, you should make sure that you’ve got a job and then see if the inventions work out.

41
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:43,120
And, look, I’m afraid we’re out of time, we have to stop now.

42
00:02:43,445 --> 00:02:45,872
I hope the talk was interesting for you all.

43
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,800
Good luck and goodbye!
